{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Down Where the Spirit Meets the Bone felt like a natural next choice because its rootsy sound connects with the blues and rock I have been listening to.",
    "Standing in the Breach appealed to me because thoughtful songwriting and familiar rock textures fit what interested me in You Should Be So Lucky."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "A Christopher Cross Christmas missed my current mood because I am not looking for holiday music, even if the performer might otherwise appeal to me.",
    "Build Me Up From Bones leaned further toward folk than I wanted, while Thick As a Brick 2 offered a progressive concept-album direction when I wanted straightforward songs."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The suggestions seemed to treat a broad connection to classic rock as enough, although the sound and song style matter more to my choice today.",
    "My occasional interest in country seemed to extend too broadly to country and folk-adjacent albums; those connections can interest me without making me want to choose them now."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "I am most drawn right now to bluesy, rootsy music with strong individual songs, rather than every style associated with the artists I have heard.",
    "An album can fit my taste and still be something I leave for later. RAM and Traveling Wilburys Collection appeal to me, but the two albums I chose felt closer to my current mood."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my interest in roots and classic rock, but sometimes stretched that interest beyond the straightforward, bluesy songwriting I want right now."
}"}
